<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharif Kabungsuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Shariff Muhammad Kabungsuwan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharif Kabungsuan was a Muslim preacher from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, of Arab descent, who arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> in the early 16th century. He spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> among the peoples of the Pulangi river basin and married into local ruling families. He is regarded as the founder of the Maguindanao Sultanate, and the rulers of both Maguindanao and Buayan traced their descent and their Islam to him.</p></div>
